function HTMLHelp00()
    DialogWindow.Help00 = [[<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><title>Help</title></head> ]] .. Style03() .. [[
  <body><div class="layout">
    <div class="h3-lP">
      <label>Main Menu Help</label>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="helpTopimage"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath .. [[\Help\Images\Main_Menu.png" width="550"></div>
      <div class="h2-lP">
        <label>Main Menu</label>
      </div>
      <div class="h1-help">
        <p>Use the Main Menu to set the drawer. The Main Menu has these areas:</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Menu buttons - </strong>These buttons open the Main Help, About, Project, Layers,
              Milling and Import menus.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Drawer Dimensions - </strong>The dimensions of the drawer opening, the slide length,
              the number of drawers and the finger count.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Material Thickness - </strong>The panel thickness and the bottom thickness.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Bits - </strong>The cabinet name and the bit for each toolpath.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Buttons at the bottom - </strong>Run and Cancel.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Each menu has a help page. The help page gives the details of each setting in that menu.</p>
        <div><hr /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="h1-help">
        <div class="h2-lP">
          <label>Drawer Dimensions</label>
        </div>
        <p>You enter the dimensions of the drawer opening. The gadget calculates the drawer from these dimensions. It
        uses the Blum clearances for undermount slides:</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help">The drawer height is the opening height minus 21 mm (13/16").</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The inside width of the drawer is the opening width minus 42 mm (1 21/32").</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The drawer length is the slide length.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Height - </strong>The vertical dimension of the drawer opening.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Width - </strong>The horizontal dimension of the drawer opening.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Slide Length - </strong>The length of the Blum undermount slide. The cabinet must
              be deep enough for this slide.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Count - </strong>The number of drawers with these dimensions.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Finger Count - </strong>The number of fingers in each joint. The minimum is 2. A
              low count gives large fingers. A high count gives small fingers.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Auto Fingers - </strong>When you tick this box, the gadget sets the finger count
              from the drawer height. It uses approximately one finger for each inch of height. The gadget then ignores
              the Finger Count box. Untick this box to enter the finger count yourself.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Test Cut - </strong>When you tick this box, the gadget cuts a test pair, not a
              drawer. The test pair is one side stub and one front stub. Use the test pair to examine the finger fit and
              the dado widths on a scrap piece. The gadget ignores Count, Width and Slide Length. It uses the Height
              that you enter, so the fingers are the same as on the real drawer. The gadget does not save this
              setting.</li>
        </ul>
        <div><hr /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="h1-help">
        <div class="h2-lP">
          <label>Material Thickness</label>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Panel Thickness - </strong>The thickness of the side, front and back panels. All
              three panels use one thickness.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Bottom Thickness - </strong>The thickness of the bottom panel. This material is
              usually thinner.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Measure each thickness with digital calipers. Enter the value to three decimal places. The joints fit
        correctly only if these values are correct.</p>
        <div><hr /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="h1-help">
        <div class="h2-lP">
          <label>Bits</label>
        </div>
        <p>The bits that you select change the time and the quality of the job. If you use only one small bit, the
        job takes more time. Use a minimum of two bits: a large bit to remove material and a small bit for the
        details.</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Cabinet Name - </strong>A name or an ID for this drawer.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Profile Bit - </strong>Cuts the outline of each part. A compression bit gives the
              best edges.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Dado Pocket Bit - </strong>Cuts the details of the dadoes and rabbets. A down-cut
              bit gives the best surface.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Dado Clearing Bit - </strong>Removes most of the material in the dadoes and
              rabbets. Use a bit that is larger than the dado pocket bit. A down-cut bit gives the best surface.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Finger Bit - </strong>Cuts the details of the fingers. A small down-cut bit gives
              the best surface. Select a bit that is correct for the joint style.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Finger Clearing Bit - </strong>Removes most of the material between the fingers.
              Use a bit that is larger than the finger bit. The bit must not be wider than a finger.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Blum Circle Bit - </strong>Cuts two 6 mm holes through the back panel for the
              Blum undermount slides. This toolpath is optional.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>Clear - </strong>Sets all bits to Tool Not Selected.</li>
          <li class="h1-help"><strong>X - </strong>Sets the bit on that line to Tool Not Selected.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>NOTE:</strong> The gadget does not make a toolpath for a bit that shows Tool Not Selected. If you
        do not use a clearing bit, do not select one.</p>
        <p>The gadget shows an error and does not continue if one of these conditions is true:</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="h1-help">The units of a bit are not the same as the units of the job.</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The finger count is too high. Each finger must be a minimum of the finger bit diameter
              / 0.70 wide.</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The finger bit is wider than a finger.</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The profile bit diameter is equal to or more than the part gap.</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The dado pocket bit is wider than the bottom thickness.</li>
          <li class="h1-help">The Blum circle bit is wider than 6 mm (0.236").</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div><hr /></div>
      <span class="helpimagesFooter"><img src="]] .. Project.AppPath ..
                              [[\Help\Images\Footer.png" width="80" height="20" alt="Page Footer"></span>
      </div>
     <div class="foot" id="FooterBox">
    <div><hr /></div>
      <div align="center"><input id="ButtonOK" class="FormButton" name="ButtonOK" type="button" value="Close"  />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>]]
    return true
end -- Function End
--  ================================================================]]
function Style03()
    return [[<style>
	.FormButton {
		font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
		font-weight: bold;
		font-size: 12px;
		white-space: nowrap;
		background-color: #663300;
		color: #FFFFFF;
	}
  .h1-help {
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    text-align: left;
    padding-right: 4px;
    padding-left: 4px;
  }
  .h2-lP {
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: left;
    padding-top: 4px;
    padding-right: 8px;
    padding-left: 18px;
  }
  .h2-lP {
		font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
		font-size: 16px;
		font-weight: bold;
		text-align: left;
		padding-top: 8px;
		padding-right: 8px;
		padding-left: 8px;
	}
  .h3-lP {
		font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
		font-size: 20px;
		font-weight: bold;
		text-align: left;
    width: 650px;
		padding-top: 18px;
		padding-right: 8px;
		padding-left: 8px;
	}
	.layout {
		background-color: white;
		color: #000000;
		overflow: auto;
		width: 99.5%;
    height: 44em;
	}
	.pad-10 {
    padding-bottom: 2em;
	}
	.foot {
		position: absolute;
		bottom: 1em;
		width: 62em;
	}
	.helpTopimage {
    position: static;
		width: 550px;
    height: 40em;
		margin: 10px 10px 10px 100px;
	}
	.helpimages {
    top: 10px;
    float: right;
		margin: 10px 10px 10px 10px;
	}
	.helpimagesX {
    top: 10px;
    float: right;
		margin: 10px 120px 10px 120px;
	}
    .helpimagesFooter {
    float: right;
    margin: 10px 313px 1px 10px;
  }
	body {
		background-color: #3a4660;
		background-position: center;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;
		font-size: 12px;
		color: #FFFFFF;
	 background-image: url(]] .. DialogWindow.myBackGround .. [[);
	}
	html {
		overflow: hidden
	}
</style>]]
end

